ounding but low causal complexity compared to environments with low confounding but high causal complexity.\"\n    ],\n    \"falsification_conditions\": [\n      \"If the agent fails to generalize to a new environment where the causal structure is identical but the marginal distributions of variables are shifted (covariate shift), H2 is falsified.\",\n      \"If the agent's internal representations are found to be dense and highly correlated (non-sparse) and do not align with known causal variables, H2 is falsified.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"H3\": {\n    \"name\": \"Energy-Based Equilibrium Seeking (Free Energy Principle)\",\n    \"mechanism\": \"The agent minimizes variational free energy $F = D_{KL}(q(z|o) || p(z|o)) - \\\\log p(o)$. The 'world model' is a generative model $p(o, z)$ that defines an energy landscape. The agent's actions are chosen to minimize the expected free energy (surprise) over future time steps. The system seeks a state of equilibrium where the internal model matches the external world, driven by the minimization of surprise rather than explicit reward maximization (reward is a special case of surprise reduction).\",\n    \"observable_predictions\": [\n      \"The agent will exhibit 'active inference' behavior: it will take actions that reduce uncertainty about the state of the world (epistemic value) even if those actions do not immediately maximize reward.\",\n      \"The agent's policy will be sensitive to the precision (inverse variance) of its beliefs: high precision beliefs will lead to rigid behavior, while low precision beliefs will lead to exploratory behavior.\",\n      \"The agent will show a preference for 'familiar' states (low entropy in the posterior) over 'novel' states, unless the novelty reduces long-term expected surprise.\"\n    ],\n    \"falsification_conditions\": [\n      \"If the agent consistently chooses actions that maximize immediate reward at the cost of increasing long-term uncertainty (violating the free energy minimization), H3 is falsified.\",\n      \"If the agent's behavior cannot be explained by a single scalar free energy function (i.e., it exhibits context-dependent preferences that cannot be unified under a single generative model), H3 is falsified.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"H0\": {\n    \"name\": \"Null Hypothesis: No Explicit World Model (Direct Policy Mapping)\",\n    \"mechanism\": \"The agent does not maintain an internal model of the environment's dynamics. Instead, it learns a direct mapping from observations to actions (or values) via end-to-end reinforcement learning. Any 'planning' is an emergent property of the policy network's depth and width, not a separate generative or predictive component. The 'world model' is a post-hoc interpretation of the policy's internal activations, not a functional component.\",\n    \"observable_predictions\": [\n      \"The agent will fail to generalize to environments with dynamics that are similar but not","errors":[],"estimated_cost":0.0,"latency_ms":9108.22,"model_deployment":"https://vllm.softsafe-tech.com/v1","model_id":"/models/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8","model_version":"/models/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8","ok":true,"prompt_sha256":"80e83d8177dc9c568b814774c23920235321d810295686760b13fd7030a8d638","prompt_tokens":74,"provider":"vllm-openai-compatible","request_id":"chatcmpl-9d03481532b8fb18","response_id":"chatcmpl-9d03481532b8fb18","retries":0,"stage":"hypotheses","temperature":0.0,"tool_calls":[],"toolset_sha256":"41a1856aa29a8c3df4bad2713b69bab84011733ff83d5c082b23612147c25d19","total_tokens":1274,"trajectory_id":"6a08b5fb886d640062dbd5a04dc4b870f2a51d3a2a39dcb6509d14cb94888ef3"}],"updated_at":"2026-11-17T14:45:41","version":"m7_discovery_v1"}